  "notes": "Sheet 0 (Paulina Jimenez, Casa Conlon, Los Cabos; 1,300 m2 beside the Sea of Cortez, 'a contemporary hacienda'): pale rendered and stone-faced walls with thick arched loggias and round stone columns, terracotta tile roofs, a pool terrace with a glass-edged infinity pool, a round pavilion on four stone columns with a deep terracotta-tiled roof reaching out over the water on a curved bridge walk (photograph 5), chandeliers and a bar inside (photographs 2, 4 and 6; not modelled), dark sea and rocks along the shore. Modelled: the main range with a tile hip roof and loggia columns, two forward wings, a tower, the pool and glass edge, the round pavilion and roof, the sea, rocks, palms. Guessed: the hacienda's plan and size (a 48 m range, wings 22 m deep, to reach 1,300 m2 over two floors), the tower. A private home placed at its town only (Los Cabos)."
